From a8e693a76917d4d6fb9590b9fc5cae9fceb85231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:33:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 62/73] toolkit: Opens submenus to the left when there is no
 room on the right.

Like Window Maker: A submenu opens to the right of its item, unless it would
extend beyond the menu's bounds; then it opens to the left. A submenu that
opened to the left opens its own submenus to the left, too. If it fits on
neither side, it opens on the side with more room. Submenus move up so they
do not extend beyond the bottom of the bounds.

wlmtk_menu_set_bounds sets the bounds, in the coordinates given by the new
wlmtk_element_get_absolute_position. The root menu, the context menus and
the window menu use the usable area of the output: The root menu is now
also kept within it when opened, not under the Dock or Clip, and the window
menu is kept within it horizontally.
